1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,520
Hello and welcome back to JD Science.

2
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:05,800
Today we are exploring plant hormones.

3
00:00:06,380 --> 00:00:09,620
We respond to light and gravity by growth.

4
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:14,380
Shoots grow towards light, which is positive phototropism and

5
00:00:14,380 --> 00:00:17,580
against gravity, which is negative geotropism.

6
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:21,060
Roots grow away from light and towards gravity.

7
00:00:21,680 --> 00:00:25,560
In shoots, auxin is destroyed by light, so the shaded

8
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:29,420
side grows faster and the shoot bends towards the light.

9
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:31,680
Etheen helps fruit ripen.

10
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:34,100
Giborelens helps seeds germinate.

11
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:37,700
Auxins are used as weed killers and rooting powders.

12
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:42,180
Giborelens can end seed dormancy, promote flowering, and

13
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:43,340
increase fruit size.

14
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,140
In a shoot exposed to light from one side, auxin is redistributed

15
00:00:48,140 --> 00:00:50,980
so that more accumulates on the shaded side.

16
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:54,840
Auxin promotes cell elongation in shoots, causing that

17
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:58,320
side to grow faster and the shoot to bend towards the light.

18
00:00:58,740 --> 00:01:02,540
It is misleading to say that light simply destroys all auxin on

19
00:01:02,540 --> 00:01:03,660
the illuminated side.

20
00:01:03,660 --> 00:01:07,300
In roots, higher auxin concentrations can inhibit

21
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:11,280
elongation, helping explain different growth responses to gravity.

22
00:01:11,640 --> 00:01:15,300
As you revise this topic, try to explain the key process in

23
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:16,140
your own words.

24
00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:20,740
What happens, why it happens, and how the structures

25
00:01:20,740 --> 00:01:22,660
involved help the process work.

26
00:01:23,240 --> 00:01:27,060
Now, pause the video and try this exam style question.

27
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:30,800
Explain why a shoot bends towards a light source.

28
00:01:31,180 --> 00:01:32,400
Here is a model answer.

29
00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:36,860
Auxin accumulates on the shaded side, promoting greater cell

30
00:01:36,860 --> 00:01:40,240
elongation there, so the shoot bends towards the light.

31
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:44,460
If this explanation has helped, please subscribe to JD Science

32
00:01:44,460 --> 00:01:50,180
for

33
00:01:50,180 --> 00:01:50,480
more research.

